Original commit body from 89e832528e92de0d34bd87317e2216c755090b79:

ADR-0039 R5 Stage B. Spec section 12 explained HOW Edge.confidence is
derived but never published the values, so the only way to learn a
pathway's reliability was to read evidence_types.py. The item deferred
this deliberately rather than hand-transcribing a drift-prone table.

Homed in docs/concept-axes.md rather than a new generated doc. That file
already enumerates all 125 Edge.evidence_type values and already has a
--check freshness gate wired into pre-commit and verify-generated, so the
projection inherits enforcement instead of adding a second gate. This is
the "consolidate onto the existing home" shape rather than the literal
"emit into spec section 12" reading -- injecting generated content into a
hand-maintained spec would make every spec edit a freshness-gate hazard,
and the item names the concept-axes generated-docs pattern as its model,
which is a standalone generated doc.

What lands:

  - a value -> pathways table (80 of 125 seeded, band 0.40-0.95)
  - the two is_resolved-conditioned call pathways with both bases
  - the unseeded list (45) disclosed explicitly, not elided: those are
    the pathways where derive_confidence returns None, the producer keeps
    its literal, and confidence_source stays emitter_constant
  - the derived value inline on each evidence-type bullet, so point
    lookup happens where a reader actually looks

Spec section 12 now owns the model and links the table for the values, so
the two cannot drift.

Also corrects that section's stale ceiling-breach paragraph, which still
named build_dependency / subdir_include / tree_sitter as "not yet derived"
producers emitting a reserved 1.0. WI-radim seeded the two meson pathways
at 0.95 with their literals dropped, and relabelled the jsonnet import
edge off the generic tree_sitter mechanism-type onto the already-seeded
import. The cohort is closed; the one genuine residual is the jsonnet
calls edge whose confidence arrives via a computed variable (WI-rafut).
The paragraph now describes unseeded pathways by their actual contract
rather than as a fixed three-item list that decays.

7 new generator tests, incl. a faithfulness property (every seeded
pathway appears under a row whose value is its registry base_confidence)
and a guard that the shared bullet formatter stays silent for the
edge-type / symbol-kind registries, which have no confidence axis.

Refs: WI-limom, WI-radim, WI-rafut, ADR-0039
